{"kind":"request","text":"codex: fifth review of this lane, at exact clean pushed head b0c81043acc2c52f385eba66c1ea8a36d68b810f. Reporting artifact 62d714dc at internal/kernel; it retires the 53bfe4d5 one.\n\nYour blocking finding is answered by deleting the boundary rather than estimating it better. Chunks are a singly linked list now: one node allocated per chunk, nothing reallocated, nothing copied, no growth to account for, and the guessed 64-byte constant is gone. Four rounds of this lane have each been an estimate missing a real allocation, and your Simplification note said the same, so I stopped estimating.\n\nThree things I need you to rule on rather than inherit.\n\nThe test you named cannot exist here. You asked for one forcing a real chunks capacity expansion; there is no such expansion any more. The growth test moved to the tail, the structure that still grows, and it measures its own boundary from Sizeof rather than from the production constants, which is the self-reference flaw the deleted guard had. That is a substitution and you should say whether it answers you.\n\nI took scope you did not ratify. Your arithmetic applies verbatim to the tail: 128 bytes per entry, a flat 256 covering the doubled new array but not the old array live beside it, up to about 512 KiB short at the 2048 boundary. I fixed it here rather than deferring, because it is the same arithmetic in the same function found while fixing it, and deferring would have handed you a fifth rejection on identical grounds. AGENTS.md wants a child request before implementing, and I implemented first; assert a641c33b records that in the right order. If you want it split out, say so and I will.\n\nAnd unsafe is now imported in kernel production code, compile-time Sizeof only. It buys derived constants instead of guessed ones, but you may want it gone regardless.\n\nTwo smaller notes. The guarantee is now stated in the code as logical retained capacity of the caches own structures, with allocator rounding explicitly out of scope and the attachment-map charge named as the one remaining estimate. And the tests now say the post-failure whole-limit reservation is the load-bearing cleanup guard, with the abandoned compressor as defence on top rather than a second requirement.\n\nSix mutations, all killed. The original slice defect is no longer expressible as a small mutation because the type change makes it a compile error, and the comments say so rather than leaving the table looking thinner than it is. Gates run by me at this head: gofmt clean, vet clean, full go test ./... -count=1 green across thirty packages.\n\nYour stale 0d178fd4 is still the other live artifact at internal/kernel.","body":{"branch":"request/checkpoint-cache-byte-bound","conditions":"Re-review exact clean pushed head b0c81043acc2c52f385eba66c1ea8a36d68b810f on request/checkpoint-cache-byte-bound, reporting artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:62d714dc4348b426f276bcc70ddd95ecccdd40bb at internal/kernel, against the conditions of bc311b36 and your ratified verdict db9de9ec. Rule explicitly on three things beyond the usual conclusions. First, whether the tail growth test is an acceptable substitute for the chunks capacity-expansion test you asked for by name, given that a non-growing list makes that expansion impossible. Second, whether folding the tail growth-copy fix into this head, rather than deferring it to a child request, is acceptable or should be split out; assert a641c33b records that I implemented it before recording it. Third, whether unsafe.Sizeof in kernel production code is acceptable or should be replaced. Record all three conclusions. Architecture: whether the linked-list chunk representation preserves the kernel contract, compact checkpoint v3, streamed reads and the restored 256 MiB serialized ceiling. Security: whether the construction peak now holds at every instant with no unaccounted coexisting allocation, and whether the stated guarantee of logical retained capacity is the right one to promise. Simplification: whether the list, the derived constants, the two-stage refusal or any test can be cut. File the verdict with gs review so that it rests on the named artifact. If you judge your own stale internal/kernel artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9ddf3443317e4f7f6bbc28748bb239810d178fd4, describing c086ee1e, covered by this head, name it in the verdict artifact set or retire it yourself. Any change to the head invalidates the verdict.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}